    <string name="JohnHortonConway">John Horton Conway</string>
    <string name="JohnHortonConway_card_description">John Horton Conway was an English mathematician who made major contributions to group theory, knot theory, number theory, combinatorial game theory, and coding theory. He is widely known for creating Conway\'s Game of Life.</string>

    <string name="the_game_of_life">Conway\'s Game of Life</string>
    <string name="GameOfLife_large_description">Conway\'s Game of Life, often simply called "Life", is a cellular automaton devised by mathematician John Horton Conway in 1970. It is a zero-player game: once the initial pattern is set, its evolution is determined entirely by the rules. The system is Turing-complete and capable of universal computation.</string>

